{{- /*
Which column of .chezmoidata/packages.toml applies to this machine: "fedora" for
Fedora, "el" for the RHEL rebuilds (Rocky, AlmaLinux, CentOS Stream) which need
EPEL and CRB, and "apt" for everything else. Shared so the two bootstrap scripts
and the test harness cannot disagree about what distro they are on.

"apt" is the fallback rather than a match, so a distro outside these families --
Arch, openSUSE, Alpine, or a machine whose osRelease is empty -- renders the apt
branch and runs a package manager it does not have. Only the three families are
supported; adding a fourth means a branch here and a column in the manifest.

Note the ordering: Rocky and Alma report idLike "rhel centos fedora", so only an
exact id of "fedora" means Fedora -- every other match in the family is "el".
*/ -}}
{{- /* toString: osRelease is empty off Linux, and `contains` rejects a nil. */ -}}
{{- $id := index .chezmoi.osRelease "id" | toString -}}
{{- $idLike := index .chezmoi.osRelease "idLike" | toString -}}
{{- $rhel := or
    (eq $id "fedora")
    (has $id (list "rhel" "rocky" "almalinux" "centos"))
    (contains "fedora" $idLike)
    (contains "rhel" $idLike) -}}
{{- if not $rhel -}}
apt
{{- else if eq $id "fedora" -}}
fedora
{{- else -}}
el
{{- end -}}
